WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.955
SailPoint's Service Desk
integration treats a provisioning

3
00:00:04.955 --> 00:00:08.562
task as complete when the mapped
ServiceNow status says so.

4
00:00:08.562 --> 00:00:12.225
So a technician sets a ticket to
Closed, and nothing was checked.

5
00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:14.250
The account might still be enabled.

6
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:15.788
The group might still be there.

7
00:00:15.788 --> 00:00:20.145
The Federal Modernization Workbook's
Book 13's rule is different:

8
00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:22.324
a success response isn't closure.

9
00:00:22.324 --> 00:00:27.150
A finding closes only when a re-read of
the target shows the intended state.

10
00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.379
Gate 6 enforces that in ServiceNow,

11
00:00:29.379 --> 00:00:34.375
for identity findings and for the tickets
the Service Desk integration opens.

12
00:00:34.375 --> 00:00:36.880
In this module you see where the fix runs,

13
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.810
and then you enforce the rule and watch
the re-read client decide six findings.
